  "conclusion": "No wrong-manager transport caused by this MIN was found in the traced controlling consumers. It is an intentionally lossy representative used to group one Candidate-directed missing Contract/week question; it is not a singleton recipient proof or a complete policy-route hash.",
  "limits": [
    "A non-minimum route change may leave the representative group key unchanged. This key must not be classified as sealing all manager addresses or policy facts.",
    "The publication-bound missing-scope fingerprint independently seals every resolved row and its saved effective-policy fingerprint. It does not itself assert current manager policy. Current manager sends use separate actual-work-date facts and current per-action CAS.",
    "A change in the minimum may change current display selection identity; existing workspace and selection CAS reject stale keys. No accepted request ID, membership, generation or clock is rewritten by the read.",
    "The Candidate request owner deliberately resolves its own real cohort from first Contract/week at the native start point, not from MIN. Its retained owner lookup/replay uses actual membership and original generation. Missing Contract/week is not partitioned by manager address.",
    "Other independent week-ending policy choices are outside this aggregate classification; no blanket claim that every manager route producer is qualified.",
    "No SQL changed. No PostgreSQL/native/provider/race execution or F23 approval is claimed."
  ],
